==English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|mum||silence}}. Recorded since 1704.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-mum's_the_word.ogg|Audio (AUS)}}

===Phrase===
{{head|en|phrase|head=[[mum]][['s]] [[the]] [[word]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} {{non-gloss definition|Indicates that something is a secret and not to be divulged.}}
#: ''She doesn't know anything about it yet, so '''mum's the word''', OK?''
#* '''1879''', [[Wikipedia:Anna_Katharine_Green|Anna Katharine Green]], ''The Leavenworth Case: A Lawyer's Story'', G. P. Putnam's Sons, page 256:
#*:  … and that ''mum'' is the word till I give you liberty to speak

